The '''2024–25 season''' was the [[List of Atlético Madrid seasons|122nd season]] in the history of [[Atlético Madrid]], and the club's 23rd consecutive season in [[La Liga]]. In addition to the [[2024–25 La Liga|domestic league]], the club participated in the [[2024–25 Copa del Rey|Copa del Rey]], the [[2024–25 UEFA Champions League|UEFA Champions League]], and the [[2025 FIFA Club World Cup|FIFA Club World Cup]].<ref name="sabcsport">{{cite news|url=https://www.sabcsport.com/soccer/news/antoine-griezmann-seals-champions-league-spot-for-atletico-madrid|title=Antoine Griezmann seals Champions League spot for Atletico Madrid|website=SABC Sport|date=16 May 2024|access-date=24 May 2024}}</ref>

Following the club's 1–0 win over [[CA Osasuna|Osasuna]] on 12 January 2025, Atlético broke its own all-time record of fourteen consecutive victories in all competitions.<ref>{{cite news |agency=The Canadian Press |date=12 January 2025 |title=Barcelona routs rival Real Madrid to claim Spanish Super Cup |url=https://www.tsn.ca/soccer/atletico-madrid-wins-record-14th-game-in-a-row-to-lead-spanish-league-at-halfway-stage-1.2234611 |access-date=14 January 2025 |website=TSN}}</ref>

